  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Core mortgage servicing operations are recovering from a period of stagnant growth driven by elevated interest rates. While the firm naturally benefits from a high-rate backdrop, the market appears slow to price in the improving outlook as servicing activity rebounds. External sentiment signals cautious optimism, with a consensus “Moderate Buy” rating among analysts, though views range from outright bearish to strong bullish. The competitive environment remains tied to rate-cycle sensitivity, but current commentary points to a turning point in end-market demand.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is leaning hard into capital allocation to address what it sees as undervaluation, using proceeds from asset sales to fund aggressive share buybacks. The repurchase program is framed as downside protection and a signal of confidence in intrinsic value. This move has drawn positive analyst attention, including an upgrade to strong-buy, though the overall brokerage posture is mixed. The strategy rests on returning capital while the stock trades at a discount, reinforcing management’s credibility as disciplined stewards of the balance sheet during the recovery.",
